From d3126230c59deb3ddfa871dd2879401e41686ffa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: p1ngb4ck <oliver@ok-it-handel.de>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 12:07:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [usb_audio,usb_host] Replace non-ASCII comment glyphs
 with ASCII

The comment banners and a few inline comments used box-drawing characters, em
dashes and a multiplication sign. Those bytes do not survive being pasted
through a terminal, which makes every patch touching these files fail to apply
for anyone transferring it that way, even when only ASCII lines changed: the
context and removal lines carry the multi-byte characters regardless.

Mechanical replacement only, comments and no code: U+2500 and U+2014 become '-',
U+00D7 becomes 'x', U+2194 becomes '<->'. Banner rules are trimmed back to the
100 column limit since one dash now takes one column instead of three.
---
 esphome/components/usb_audio/uac_types.h      | 30 ++++++------
 esphome/components/usb_audio/usb_audio.cpp    | 48 +++++++++----------
 esphome/components/usb_audio/usb_audio.h      | 44 ++++++++---------
 esphome/components/usb_host/usb_host.h        | 24 +++++-----
 .../components/usb_host/usb_host_client.cpp   | 12 ++---
 .../usb_host/usb_host_component.cpp           |  8 ++--
 6 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 83 deletions(-)

